    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Is Inflation Back?\"\nsubtitle: \"Prices are rising faster again, mostly because of gas. And for the first time in years, paychecks are falling behind.\"\nauthor: \"SixtyEight95\"\ndate: \"2026-11-19\"\ncategories: [inflation, cost of living, wages, energy]\nimage: infographic.png\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\nAfter the 2021–2023 price surge finally cooled, a lot of people hoped inflation was behind us. This year, it\nstarted climbing again. We looked at the government's own numbers to see how big the rebound is, what's\ndriving it, and what it means for your paycheck.\n\n## The short answer\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\nPrices are up **4.1%** from a year ago (October 2026), up from **2.7%** in\nFebruary 2026. Most of the jump is **energy**: gasoline is up **37.4%**. Without food and energy,\ninflation is a calmer **2.9%**.\n\nBut it's enough to bite: pay is up only **3.3%**, so the average paycheck now buys **less** than it did a\nyear ago for the first time since early 2023.\n:::\n\n## The rebound\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-a0e0788cc83ffdb0c517\" style=\"width:100%;height:417px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-a0e0788cc83ffdb0c517\">{\"x\":{\"data\":[{\"x\":[17755.5,20868.5],\"y\":[2,2],\"text\":\"\",\"type\":\"scatter\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"line\":{\"width\":1.8897637795275593,\"color\":\"rgba(153,153,153,1)\",\"dash\":\"dash\"},\"hoveron\":\"points\",\"showlegend\":false,\"xaxis\":\"x\",\"yaxis\":\"y\",\"hoverinfo\":\"text\",\"frame\":null},{\"x\":[20512,20512],\"y\":[-0.24085668639119207,9.4184190930818463],\"text\":\"\",\"type\":\"scatter\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"line\":{\"width\":1.8897637795275593,\"color\":\"rgba(214,158,46,1)\",\"dash\":\"dot\"},\"hoveron\":\"points\",\"showlegend\":false,\"xaxis\":\"x\",\"yaxis\":\"y\",\"hoverinfo\":\"text\",\"frame\":null},{\"x\":[17897,17928,