",\"5.0\",\"7.5\"],\"tickvals\":[0,2.5,5,7.5],\"categoryorder\":\"array\",\"categoryarray\":[\"0.0\",\"2.5\",\"5.0\",\"7.5\"],\"nticks\":null,\"ticks\":\"\",\"tickcolor\":null,\"ticklen\":3.6529680365296811,\"tickwidth\":0,\"showticklabels\":true,\"tickfont\":{\"color\":\"rgba(77,77,77,1)\",\"family\":\"\",\"size\":11.68949771689498},\"tickangle\":-0,\"showline\":false,\"linecolor\":null,\"linewidth\":0,\"showgrid\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"rgba(235,235,235,1)\",\"gridwidth\":0.66417600664176002,\"zeroline\":false,\"anchor\":\"x\",\"title\":{\"text\":\"Change from a year earlier (%)\",\"font\":{\"color\":\"rgba(0,0,0,1)\",\"family\":\"\",\"size\":14.611872146118724}},\"hoverformat\":\".2f\"},\"shapes\":[{\"type\":\"rect\",\"fillcolor\":null,\"line\":{\"color\":null,\"width\":0,\"linetype\":[]},\"yref\":\"paper\",\"xref\":\"paper\",\"x0\":0,\"x1\":1,\"y0\":0,\"y1\":1}],\"showlegend\":true,\"legend\":{\"bgcolor\":null,\"bordercolor\":null,\"borderwidth\":0,\"font\":{\"color\":\"rgba(0,0,0,1)\",\"family\":\"\",\"size\":11.68949771689498},\"title\":{\"text\":\"\",\"font\":{\"color\":\"rgba(0,0,0,1)\",\"family\":\"\",\"size\":14.611872146118724}},\"orientation\":\"h\",\"y\":1.0800000000000001},\"hovermode\":\"closest\",\"barmode\":\"relative\"},\"config\":{\"doubleClick\":\"reset\",\"modeBarButtonsToAdd\":[\"hoverclosest\",\"hovercompare\"],\"showSendToCloud\":false,\"displayModeBar\":false},\"source\":\"A\",\"attrs\":{\"22b421893288\":{\"yintercept\":{},\"type\":\"scatter\"},\"22b41592653\":{\"xintercept\":{}},\"22b412a7d51\":{\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"colour\":{},\"text\":{}}},\"cur_data\":\"22b421893288\",\"visdat\":{\"22b421893288\":[\"function (y) \",\"x\"],\"22b41592653\":[\"function (y) \",\"x\"],\"22b412a7d51\":[\"function (y) \",\"x\"]},\"highlight\":{\"on\":\"plotly_click\",\"persistent\":false,\"dynamic\":false,\"selectize\":false,\"opacityDim\":0.20000000000000001,\"selected\":{\"opacity\":1},\"debounce\":0},\"shinyEvents\":[\"plotly_hover\",\"plotly_click\",\"plotly_selected\",\"plotly_relayout\",\"plotly_brushed\",\"plotly_brushing\",\"plotly_clickannotation\",\"plotly_doubleclick\",\"plotly_deselect\",\"plotly_afterplot\",\"plotly_sunburstclick\"],\"base_url\":\"https://plot.ly\"},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe dashed line is the Federal Reserve's 2% target. The dotted line marks the U.S. and Israeli strike on Iran in\nlate February 2026, which disrupted oil shipping through the Strait of Hormuz. Notice that the red line (all prices)\njumped right after, while the teal line (everything except food and energy) barely moved. That tells you this\nrebound is mostly about energy, not a broad-based surge like 2022.\n\n## What's driving it\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\nTable: Consumer and producer price indexes, October 2026 vs. a year earlier. Source: BLS via FRED.\n\n|Category                               | Change from a year ago|\n|:--------------------------------------|----------------------:|\n|Gasoline                               |                  37.4%|\n|All energy (gas, electricity, heating) |                  21.2%|\n|Housing costs (shelter)                |                   3.5%|\n|Food                                   |                   2.9%|\n|Everything except food & energy        |                   2.9%|\n|All prices                             |                   4.1%|\n|Wholesale prices (producer prices)     |                   6.5%|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nTwo things to watch:\n\n- **Wholesale prices are up 6.5%.** Producer prices measure what businesses pay. When those rise\n  faster than consumer prices, some of it tends to show up on store shelves later.\n- **Food is starting to climb.** Food prices rose 2.9% over the year, and higher fuel and shipping costs\n  can push grocery prices up with a delay.\n\n## What it means for your paycheck\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"plotly html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwi